# The FF Collective — product doctrine

This app is **The FF Collective** (not “Open Board” in user-facing copy).

**Live URL:** https://theffcollective.vercel.app/  
**Source of truth for strings:** `src/lib/brand.ts` — prefer shared constants over new one-off copy.

## North star

Best half-PPR projections **because** the public contributes inputs; we review and republish together.  
Formula: **team offense + player share + player efficiency = fantasy points**.

Prefer **contribute / input / collective model / review & republish** (ownership).  
Avoid ticket language: “looks wrong,” “submit a bug,” “propose edit,” “edit projection” as the primary CTA.

## Verb map (UI)

| Don’t ship | Do ship |
|---|---|
| Edit projection | Contribute (to this / team offense / share / efficiency) |
| Propose / Propose edit | Contribute / Contribute an input |
| Submit edit | Submit contribution |
| looks wrong | disagree with an input / improve an input |

Keep **Community outlook / Add player|team outlook** as the written-take lane (not a number pin).

## When changing UI

1. Reuse `BRAND_*` from `brand.ts` for callouts, loops, success, pie intros.
2. Preserve the contribute loop: inspect pieces → contribute input → review & republish.
3. Don’t rename internal IDs (`open_board`, API `edits`, code symbols) unless asked — only user-facing labels.
4. Mockups under `/preview` are optional; live `/` must stay on-brand.

## External / marketing copy

Name the product **The FF Collective**, link https://theffcollective.vercel.app/, invite people to **contribute** (not “submit a bug / edit because wrong”).
